|~ qlang operand catalog — container family. Each operand BindStep
   below sits directly under the per-site error tags it raises;
   the operand's `:throws` Vec references those tags by name. ~|

:count
  |~~ Returns the number of elements. Polymorphic over Vec
      (length), Set (size), and Map (entry count).

      ~([1 2 3] | count | eq 3)
      ~(#[:a :b] | count | eq 2)
      ~({:x 1 :y 2 :z 3} | count | eq 3)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/count
            :category :containerReducer
            :subject [:vec :set :map]
            :returns :number}

::CountSubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ Subject of `count` must be Vec, Set, or Map.
      ~(
        42 | count
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::CountSubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:empty
  |~~ Returns true if the container has zero elements, false
      otherwise. Polymorphic over Vec, Set, and Map.

      ~([] | empty | eq true)
      ~([1] | empty | eq false)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/empty
            :category :containerReducer
            :subject [:vec :set :map]
            :returns :boolean}

::EmptySubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ Subject of `empty` must be Vec, Set, or Map.
      ~(
        42 | empty
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::EmptySubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:every
  |~~ Returns true iff every item of the container satisfies the
      predicate. Polymorphic over Vec / Set / Map, a map's elements
      being its values: the predicate fires per element with it as
      pipeValue, and a conduit of one parameter [:x] binds it as a
      captured-arg. Short-circuits on the first falsy result.
      Vacuously true for empty containers.

      ~([2 4 6 8] | every ~(gt 0) | eq true)
      ~([1 2 3] | every ~(gt 2) | eq false)
      ~([2 4 6] | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | every ~(@pos) | eq true)
      ~([] | every ~(gt 0) | eq true)
      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | every ~(gt 0) | eq true)
      ~({:a 1 :b -2 :c 3} | every ~(gt 0) | eq false)
      ~({:a 1 :b 2} | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | every ~(@pos) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/every
            :category :containerSelector
            :subject [:vec :set :map]
            :returns :boolean
            :modifiers [:predicateLambda]}

::EverySubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ Subject of `every` must be Vec, Set, or Map.
      ~(
        42 | every ~(gt 0)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::EverySubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::EveryPredArityInvalidError
  |~~ `every` requires a predicate conduit with 0 or 1 params (`[:x]` binds the element, a map's value among them).
      ~(
        [1 2] | :@kv [:k :v] true | every ~(@kv)
        !| [type /conduitName /actualArity]
        |  eq [::EveryPredArityInvalidError :@kv 2]
       )
  ~~|

::EveryPredicateNotQuoteError
  |~~ The predicate of `every` is code it runs on each element, so it takes a
      quote, `every ~(gt 0)`; a value computed at the call is refused.
      ~(
        [1 2 3] | every (count | gt 1)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::EveryPredicateNotQuoteError ::boolean]
       )
  ~~|

:any
  |~~ Returns true iff at least one item of the container
      satisfies the predicate. Polymorphic over Vec / Set / Map,
      a map's elements being its values, with the same dispatch as
      every. Short-circuits on the first truthy result. Vacuously false
      for empty containers.

      ~([1 2 3] | any ~(gt 2) | eq true)
      ~([1 2 3] | any ~(gt 99) | eq false)
      ~([1 2 3] | :@big [:v] (v | gt 2) | any ~(@big) | eq true)
      ~([] | any ~(gt 0) | eq false)
      ~({:a -1 :b 0 :c 2} | any ~(gt 0) | eq true)
      ~({:a -1 :b 2} | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | any ~(@pos) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/any
            :category :containerSelector
            :subject [:vec :set :map]
            :returns :boolean
            :modifiers [:predicateLambda]}

::AnySubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ Subject of `any` must be Vec, Set, or Map.
      ~(
        42 | any ~(gt 0)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AnySubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::AnyPredArityInvalidError
  |~~ `any` requires a predicate conduit with 0 or 1 params (`[:x]` binds the element, a map's value among them).
      ~(
        [1 2] | :@kv [:k :v] true | any ~(@kv)
        !| [type /conduitName /actualArity]
        |  eq [::AnyPredArityInvalidError :@kv 2]
       )
  ~~|

::AnyPredicateNotQuoteError
  |~~ The predicate of `any` is code it runs on each element, so it takes a
      quote, `any ~(gt 2)`; a value computed at the call is refused.
      ~(
        [1 2 3] | any (count | gt 1)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::AnyPredicateNotQuoteError ::boolean]
       )
  ~~|

:filter
  |~~ Keeps items of the container where the predicate evaluates
      truthy, returning a new container of the same shape. A map's
      elements are its values: the predicate sees the value, and the
      entries whose value passes keep their keys. A conduit of one
      parameter [:x] binds the element as its captured-arg; the joint
      test of a key with its value reads the keys, `m | keys | filter
      ~(…)`, and `at` the value of each.

      ~([1 2 3 4 5] | filter ~(gt 2) | eq [3 4 5])
      ~([{:age 25} {:age 15}] | filter ~(/age | gte 18) | eq [{:age 25}])
      ~([1 -2 3] | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | filter ~(@pos) | eq [1 3])
      ~(#[1 2 3 4 5] | filter ~(gt 2) | eq #[3 4 5])
      ~(#[1 -2 3] | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | filter ~(@pos) | eq #[1 3])
      ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3} | filter ~(gt 1) | eq {:b 2 :c 3})
      ~({:a 1 :b -2 :c 3} | :@pos [:v] (v | gt 0) | filter ~(@pos) | eq {:a 1 :c 3})
      ~({} | filter ~(gt 0) | eq {})
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/filter
            :category :containerSelector
            :subject [:vec :set :map]
            :returns [:vec :set :map]
            :modifiers [:predicateLambda]}

::FilterSubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ Subject of `filter` must be Vec, Set, or Map.
      ~(
        42 | filter ~(gt 0)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::FilterSubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

::FilterPredArityInvalidError
  |~~ `filter` requires a predicate conduit with 0 or 1 params (`[:x]` binds the element, a map's value among them).
      ~(
        [1 2] | :@kv [:k :v] true | filter ~(@kv)
        !| [type /conduitName /actualArity]
        |  eq [::FilterPredArityInvalidError :@kv 2]
       )
  ~~|

::FilterPredicateNotQuoteError
  |~~ The predicate of `filter` is code it runs on each element, so it takes a
      quote, `filter ~(gt 1)`; a value computed at the call is refused.
      ~(
        [1 2 3] | filter (count | gt 1)
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::FilterPredicateNotQuoteError ::boolean]
       )
  ~~|
